So hamara MCP conceptually stronger hai.

The reason is simple:

youtube-conversation is optimized for one user + one Chrome session + YouTube conversation.
Our MCP is being built as a general-purpose YouTube research engine.

Current code actually backs that up: the router has separate provider chains for search, metadata and transcripts, with health-aware failover and single-flight coalescing.

And the circuit breaker is capability-specific rather than just provider-wide, which is a pretty serious architectural advantage.

BUT - ek jagah YouTube Conversation humse better hai

Reliability of transcript acquisition from a user's own session.

Uska Chrome-based approach YouTube ke already authenticated/browser-visible environment ko use karta hai. Hamara MCP InnerTube/yt-dlp based hai, so YouTube changes, bot detection, rate limits, etc. ka risk hai.

That's why our architecture has:

YouTube
                │
       ┌────────┼────────┐
       ▼        ▼        ▼
   InnerTube  yt-dlp  Commercial
       │        │        │
       └────────┼────────┘
                ▼
        Provider Router
                ▼
        Circuit Breaker
                ▼
          Cache / Search
                ▼
       Research Engine

That's much more ambitious.

🔥 Final verdict

Agar question hai: "Kaunsa zyada powerful hai?" → Hamara MCP.

"Kaunsa ChatGPT mein YouTube video se instantly baat karne ke liye polished hai?" → YouTube Conversation.

"Kaunsa ek proper standalone YouTube research infrastructure ban sakta hai?" → Hamara MCP, by a pretty big margin.

Bas ek condition hai: hamare MCP ko abhi prove karna baaki hai ki ye architecture real-world YouTube failures ke against utna hi reliable hai jitna design paper par dikhta hai.

Aur isi liye 2nd build ke baad mujhe feature #3 add karne se pehle aggressive reliability testing karni chahiye lagti hai.

