# PHASE 8 — PROVIDER FAILOVER

Test provider behavior under:

- normal operation
- provider failure
- invalid video
- unavailable transcript
- timeout
- malformed provider response
- repeated failures

Verify:

```text
Primary fails
    ↓
Fallback attempted
    ↓
Fallback succeeds
    ↓
Correct result returned
```

Verify that:

- provider errors don't leak incorrectly
- healthy providers remain usable
- failover doesn't cause cache contamination
- provider health state is correct

---

# PHASE 9 — CIRCUIT BREAKER

Test:

- repeated provider failures
- threshold crossing
- circuit opening
- requests while open
- recovery
- half-open behavior if implemented
- successful recovery
- capability isolation

Important:

A transcript failure must NOT unnecessarily break:

- search
- metadata
- other independent capabilities

Test this explicitly.

---

# PHASE 10 — SINGLE-FLIGHT

Verify request coalescing.

Run:

```text
5 identical requests
10 identical requests
25 identical requests
50 identical requests if safe
```

Verify:

```text
N client requests
        ↓
1 upstream operation
        ↓
N responses
```

Verify:

- all callers receive correct data
- no request mixing
- no deadlocks
- no leaked futures
- exceptions propagate correctly
- cache interaction is correct

---

# PHASE 11 — CACHE TESTING

