# 🚨 BUG SEVERITY CLASSIFICATION

For every newly discovered bug classify:

### P0 — Critical

- data corruption
- security compromise
- complete system failure
- destructive behavior

### P1 — High

- major public functionality broken
- severe cache contamination
- request mixing
- repeated crashes
- major security issue

### P2 — Medium

- important functionality unreliable
- significant incorrect results
- serious performance/reliability issue

### P3 — Low

- minor validation issue
- documentation discrepancy
- edge-case UX issue
- non-critical feature limitation

Every bug must include:

```text
BUG-ID
Severity
Title
Affected component
Exact reproduction
Expected behavior
Actual behavior
Root cause
Evidence
Frequency
Impact
Suggested fix direction
```

Do NOT fix it.

---

# 🧾 EVIDENCE REQUIREMENT

For every important failure collect evidence:

- exact command
- input
- output
- traceback if applicable
- relevant logs
- relevant source location
- reproducibility count

Never report:

> "probably broken"

Instead report:

> "Reproduced 4/4 times with X input; expected Y, received Z."

---

# 🚫 DO NOT CHEAT THE TESTING

Do NOT:

- mark tests PASS based only on source inspection
- reuse old results without revalidation
- skip difficult phases
- hide flaky failures
- ignore inconsistent results
- silently modify production code
- change tests merely to make them pass
- weaken assertions
- suppress exceptions
- delete failing tests
- alter production configuration just to manufacture a PASS

If something cannot be tested, say:

```text
NOT TESTABLE — reason
```

---

