# 🔥 FINAL RULE

The objective of this sprint is **not to make the report look good**.

The objective is to break the system if it can be broken.

Be skeptical.

Try unusual inputs.

Try concurrency.

Try conflicting requests.

Try cache races.

Try provider failures.

Try malformed inputs.

Try multilingual requests.

Try transport failures.

Try repeated requests.

Try simultaneous agents.

If everything passes, that's excellent — but only after attempting to find real failures.

**Do not modify production code during this sprint.**

First:

> TEST → BREAK → REPRODUCE → DOCUMENT

Then we will start a separate:

> FIX → REGRESSION → VERIFY → RELEASE

sprint.

Iske baad jo **FINAL_QA_REPORT.md** aayegi, woh next step ke liye perfect base hogi. Agar naye bugs milte hain, phir hum us report ke basis par **targeted fix prompt** banayenge—blindly code touch nahi karenge.

