# Step 3 — Redis actually MCP mein karega kya?

Current architecture roughly:

```text
                 ┌──────────────┐
Request ────────►│   MCP Tools  │
                 └──────┬───────┘
                        │
                 ┌──────▼───────┐
                 │   Services   │
                 └──────┬───────┘
                        │
                 ┌──────▼───────┐
                 │ Cache Layer   │
                 └──────┬───────┘
                        │
             ┌──────────┴──────────┐
             ▼                     ▼
        SQLite Cache          Redis Cache
```

Aur config se choose hoga:

```env
CACHE_BACKEND=sqlite
```

ya:

```env
CACHE_BACKEND=redis
```

So **Redis replace nahi karega MCP ko**. Redis sirf cache backend hoga.

---

# Step 4 — Redis mein kya cache hoga?

Tumhare MCP ke architecture ke according primarily:

### Search

```text
search:<query>:<filters>
```

### Metadata

```text
video:<video_id>
```

### Transcript

```text
transcript:<video_id>:<language>:<fallback>:<translation>
```

### Negative cache

Agar YouTube request fail hui:

```text
negative:<...>
```

### Single-flight

Ye important hai:

```text
25 agents
   │
   ├── request A
   ├── request A
   ├── request A
   ├── ...
   └── request A
          │
          ▼
       Redis/cache
          │
          ▼
    ONE upstream request
```

Yahi tumhare existing Phase 25 testing ka important part tha.

