## 🔥 Mere hisaab se best setup

Tumhare MCP ke liye:

**Development**

```env
CACHE_BACKEND=sqlite
```

**Redis integration testing**

```env
CACHE_BACKEND=redis
```

**Production**

```env
CACHE_BACKEND=redis
```

Aur architecture ideally:

```text
                 YouTube Research MCP
                         │
                    Cache Interface
                         │
             ┌───────────┴───────────┐
             │                       │
          SQLite                   Redis
       Development              Production
             │                       │
          local DB               cloud Redis
```

Isse tumhara MCP **single-machine cache** se **shared/distributed cache** architecture ki taraf move karega — aur ye especially useful hoga jab multiple OpenCode agents / MCP clients simultaneously same server ko hit karenge. 🚀

### Ab next step

Agar tum **Upstash Redis** use karne wale ho, toh account/database create karke **Redis connection URL** le aao. **Actual URL mujhe yahan paste karne ki zarurat nahi hai.** Phir main tumhe **ek full copy-paste OpenCode prompt** de sakta hoon jo existing codebase ko read karke Redis implementation, integration, security, tests, failover, TTL, concurrency aur production-readiness sab systematically handle karwaye.

